    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting high-SB upside against vulnerable rotations. The standout play of the day is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.12), whose efficiency is bolstered by a favorable matchup against Fedde (5.37 xERA). His profile is maximized by a 93% SB-success probability due to the opponent's slow delivery, offsetting his lower spot in the lineup. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (73.14) provides elite value; he benefits from a positive platoon split and an 87% SB-probability against Ober, making him a cornerstone of today's production. **Carson Benge** (67.23) also emerges as a strong start, capitalizing on a 6.75 xERA matchup against Rodr\u00edguez, E to punch well above his base projection.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing high-efficiency slots over volume. **Chase Meidroth** (46.83) was the hardest exclusion today, ultimately benched because his matchup against Rea does not yield the same ceiling as the rest of our utility core. While **Junior Caminero** (61.59) slots into our UTIL spot due to his consistent base, he narrowly edged out the lower-projected options. We are closely monitoring the risk inherent in facing Skenes today; both **Trea Turner** (49.78) and **Kyle Schwarber** (48.24) face a daunting challenge against his elite arm. Despite the skill-based penalties in their scores, their top-of-the-order positioning forces us to keep them active to protect our R/RBI potential. \n\nFinally, a note on situational adjustments: **Dillon Dingler** (40.07) and **Colt Keith** (53.09) are facing Gausman in an environment complicated by an inward wind, which has suppressed their output relative to expectations. Conversely, **Hyeseong Kim** (53.66) receives a slight bump from favorable winds tonight, providing a stable floor for our middle-infield production. We continue to hold **Zac Veen** in the minors as he works toward a potential call-up, while **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** remain on the periphery, awaiting shifts in health or performance that would necessitate a promotion to the active starting nine.",
